/** @mainpage Qore imagemagick Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section imagemagickintro ImageMagick Module Introduction

    The \c imagemagick module provides comprehensive image processing and manipulation capabilities
    for %Qore by wrapping the ImageMagick MagickWand C API.

    To use this module, use the \c %%requires directive as follows:
    @code{.py}
%requires imagemagick
    @endcode

    This module provides the following classes:
    - @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage "MagickImage": the main image class for loading,
      manipulating, and saving images
    - @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickDrawing "MagickDrawing": vector graphics drawing class

    @section imagemagickreq ImageMagick Module Requirements

    This module requires:
    - %Qore 2.0+
    - ImageMagick 7.0+ with MagickWand development libraries

    @section imagemagickquickstart Quick Start

    @par Loading and resizing an image:
    @code{.py}
%requires imagemagick

MagickImage img("photo.jpg");
img.resize(800, 600, "Lanczos");
img.writeFile("photo_resized.jpg");
    @endcode

    @par Format conversion:
    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("document.png");
binary jpeg_data = img.toData("JPEG");
    @endcode

    @par Applying effects:
    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("photo.jpg");
img.charcoal(1.0, 0.5);
img.writeFile("charcoal.jpg");
    @endcode

    @par Drawing shapes and text:
    @code{.py}
MagickDrawing dw();
dw.setFillColor("blue");
dw.rectangle(10.0, 10.0, 100.0, 100.0);
dw.setFillColor("red");
dw.setFontSize(24.0);
dw.annotation(50.0, 150.0, "Hello!");

MagickImage img(300, 300, "white");
img.draw(dw);
img.writeFile("drawing.png");
    @endcode

    @par Creating thumbnails:
    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("photo.jpg");
img.thumbnail(200, 200);
img.sharpen(0.0, 1.0);
img.setCompressionQuality(85);
img.writeFile("thumb.jpg");
    @endcode

    @par Working with metadata:
    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("photo.jpg");
hash<ImageInfo> info = img.getInfo();
printf("Size: %dx%d, Format: %s\n", info.width, info.height, info.format);
    @endcode

    @section imagemagickformats Supported Image Formats

    ImageMagick supports over 200 image formats including PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, TIFF, WebP,
    SVG, PDF, and many more. The available formats depend on your ImageMagick installation
    and its configured delegates.

    @section imagemagickfilters Filter Types

    The following filter types are available for resize operations:
    | Filter | Description |
    |--------|-------------|
    | Lanczos | High quality (default, recommended for most uses) |
    | Mitchell | Balanced sharpness and ringing |
    | Catrom | Catmull-Rom spline (good for reduction) |
    | Gaussian | Gaussian curve |
    | Box | Nearest neighbor (for pixel art upscaling) |
    | Triangle | Bilinear interpolation |
    | Point | Nearest neighbor (fastest) |
    | Cubic | Cubic interpolation |

    @section imagemagickcolorspaces Colorspaces

    Supported colorspaces include: sRGB, RGB, CMYK, Gray, HSL, HSV, Lab, LCH, YCbCr,
    and many others.

    @section imagemagickdataprovider Data Provider API

    The \c ImageMagickDataProvider module provides integration with the %Qore data provider
    framework for use with Qorus. See @ref imagemagickdataproviderintro for details.

    @section imagemagickerrors Error Handling

    All errors are raised as \c IMAGEMAGICK-ERROR exceptions with descriptive messages
    from the ImageMagick library.

